meta {
  name: Get Bulk Email Recipients
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{notificationsBaseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/bulk-email/{{bulkEmailJobGuid}}/recipients?page=1&size=50
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  size: 50
  ~status: Failed
  ~search: example.com
}

vars:pre-request {
  bulkEmailJobGuid: e6c63664-de00-415a-b0a1-9fb5ac3fba8e
}

docs {
  The per-person breakdown for one bulk job: one row per recipient with the address,
  send status, attempt count, and last error. This is where "did THIS student get it,
  and if not why" gets answered — Get Bulk Email gives the totals, this gives the rows
  behind them.
  
  Rows come from OutboundEmails filtered to this job id. Transactional rows (no job id)
  are unreachable here by construction.
  
  Set bulkEmailJobGuid from a List Bulk Emails response.
  
  Query params:
    page   - default 1
    size   - default 50; clamped to 1..200 (note: ceiling is 200 here, vs 100 on the job list)
    status - Queued | Sending | Sent | Failed | Suppressed  -- the RECIPIENT status enum
             (OutboundEmailStatus), NOT the job status enum. Bound by name.
    search - case-insensitive LIKE against toEmail
  
  Success (200): data is a PagedResult of BulkEmailRecipientStatusDto:
    emailGuid   - the OutboundEmails row id; distinct from jobGuid and recipientGuid.
                  There is no single-row GET for it.
    toEmail     - the resolved address (the application's EmailId)
    recipientType   - Student | Employee (always Student in practice)
    recipientGuid   - the student GUID from the original selections
    status, attempts, lastError, processedDate
  
  attempts increments at CLAIM time, not send time. A permanently-undeliverable address
  (malformed / provider-rejected) is still retried up to attempts=5 before going Failed
  rather than failing on the first try — against real SES that is five bounces, not one.
  
  404 not_found "Bulk email not found." - no BulkEmailJobs row with that GUID.
  A job that exists but has zero recipient rows is a 200 with items: [], not a 404.
  401 unauthorized - no valid erp_access cookie.
}
